    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 545 of 2003",
    "lawSection": "Social Services",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7826\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 545 of the laws of 2003,\namending the social services law relating to the assisted living\nprogram, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n PURPOSE :  The purpose of this legislation is to provide for the\nexpansion of assisted living programs unable to meet the demand for\navailable beds.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :  Section one extends the demonstration\nprogram allowing for the expansion of assisted living programs unable\nto meet the demand for available beds.\n\nSection two states this bill shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :  This bill continues the demonstration program\nestablished in Chapter 593 of the laws of 2003 and amended by Chapter\n545 of the laws of 2005, to allow certain assisted living facilities\nto increase their number of assisted living beds by up to thirty\npercent of its approved bed level to accommodate individuals awaiting\nplacement into the assisted living program.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :  Chapter 593 of the Laws of 2005\nChapter 545 of the Laws of 2003\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  This act shall take effect immediately and shall be\ndeemed repealed September 1, 2013.\n",
